    "error": "AssertionError(('unguarded_effect_argument', 'global_var:nesnd_hus_registration_serial', 'HUS', 'preview'))",
    "explanation": "The first HUS choice enters `nesnd_hus_choose_registration` and then `nesnd_hus_allocate_registration_epoch` (starts at L52). That helper writes a missing global serial and later reads `global_var:nesnd_hus_registration_serial` into the local epoch; further statements read the newly written local epoch. A first-open preview has neither value, and hidden_effect does not establish those variables for its later expressions. The normal execution positive control allocates epoch 1 with a one-year global wait and rejects a second click; the preview-only read fails. This is the same write-before-read preview pattern already prohibited by the project validation contract. A repair must make each preview-visible numeric expression independently readable via guarded values/fallbacks, while preserving real execution's serial allocation and immutable deadline. Moving the same expressions into another hidden block is insufficient.",
